{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts security deposit cap, interest and return","requirement":"A lessor may not require a security deposit above one month's rent, must hold it in a separate interest-bearing account, pay the tenant 5% interest per year, and return the deposit with accrued interest within 30 days after the tenancy ends.","key_value":"1 month's rent cap; 5% per year interest; return within 30 days","coverage_conditions":"Residential real property tenancies in Massachusetts. The text states no building-age, unit-count or owner-type limits.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"The successor-in-interest liability rule does not apply to a city or town that acquires title under chapter sixty, a foreclosing mortgagee, or a mortgagee in possession that is a chartered financial institution.","penalty":"Lessor forfeits the right to retain any part of the deposit; for failure to comply with subsection (6)(a), (d) or (e) the tenant is awarded three times the deposit or balance plus 5% interest, court costs and attorney's fees.","effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(iii) a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2);","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D052-01","doc_id":"D052","jurisdiction":"MA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Massachusetts cap on upfront amounts a tenant may be charged","requirement":"At or before a tenancy begins, a lessor or agent may require only first and last month's rent, one month's rent as a security deposit, and key-and-lock cost; an optional deposit-alternative fee is capped at one month's rent.","key_value":"first + last month's rent + 1 month's rent deposit + key and lock cost; deposit-alternative fee max 1 month's rent","coverage_conditions":"Any residential tenancy in Massachusetts; covers lessors and their agents. No building-age, unit-count or owner-type limits stated.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-08-01","citation":"G.L. c. 186, § 15B","quoted_span":"(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: (i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, (ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
